---
import DiagramLabel from './DiagramLabel.astro'
// Judge SELECTION, which is not judge calibration, and the figure exists to hold those two apart.
//
// What Atlas actually measured: nine candidate judges over a 20 case selection set whose ground
// truth is fixed by construction (10 PASS / 10 FAIL, so a judge that always says PASS scores 50%).
// The OpenAI arm ran every case under two prompt conditions, so its denominator is 40; the
// Anthropic arm ran one condition, so its denominator is 20. Reproduce the set and its balance with
//   uv run python -c "from judge import selection_cases as s; print(len(s.CASES), s.balance())"
//   -> 20  "20 cases: 10 PASS / 10 FAIL (50% PASS, so an always PASS judge scores 50%)"
//
// What Atlas has NOT measured: agreement with a human. There are zero human labels in the repo,
// `judge/labels/` does not exist, and `judge/contract.py` treats a JudgeContract with no
// CalibrationRecord as UNLICENSED, so `require_licensed()` refuses. The 0.60 bar below is
// `judge.calibration.AUTOMATION_BAR` (Landis and Koch 1977, the floor of "substantial"), and it has
// nothing standing against it yet. `judge/queue/items.jsonl` holds the 50 answers waiting to be
// labelled: wc -l judge/queue/items.jsonl -> 50.
//
// An earlier draft of this figure rendered a 28 case human agreement table moving from kappa 0.21 to
// 0.85. No such measurement exists. It is gone rather than restyled.
const arms = {
  openai: {
    label: 'OpenAI',
    trials: 40,
    note: 'every case under both prompt conditions, so 40 verdicts per candidate',
    rows: [
      { model: 'gpt-5.6-luna', score: 40, chosen: true, detail: 'cheapest of the four that tied at the top' },
      { model: 'gpt-5.4-mini', score: 36, chosen: false, detail: 'last of the nine candidates run' },
    ],
  },
  anthropic: {
    label: 'Anthropic',
    trials: 20,
    note: 'one prompt condition, so 20 verdicts per candidate',
    rows: [
      { model: 'claude-opus-5', score: 20, chosen: true, detail: 'the only Claude model to match luna' },
      { model: 'claude-sonnet-5', score: 18, chosen: false, detail: 'missed the same case gpt-5.4-mini missed' },
    ],
  },
}
const BAR = 0.6 // judge.calibration.AUTOMATION_BAR, as a fraction of the 0..1 kappa track
const armData = JSON.stringify(arms)
---

<figure class="not-prose my-10 border border-border-dark bg-surface rounded-lg p-5" data-jc data-arms={armData} data-inview>
  <div class="mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
    <DiagramLabel label="Judge selection is not judge calibration" />
    <div class="h-px flex-1 bg-border-dark"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- The licence strip. The bar is real and lives in the code; the needle is missing, because
       nothing has been measured against it. That absence is the honest state, so it is drawn. -->
  <div class="jc-licence mb-5">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 mb-2">
      <span class="font-mono text-3xl text-text-muted">κ ?</span>
      <span class="font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-error">unlicensed</span>
      <span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted sm:ml-auto">human labels <span class="text-text-primary">0</span> · queued for labelling <span class="text-text-primary">50</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="jc-track relative h-2.5 w-full overflow-hidden">
      <div class="jc-bar absolute inset-y-0" style={`left:${BAR * 100}%`}></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative mt-1 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">
      <span>κ 0</span>
      <span class="hidden sm:inline absolute -translate-x-1/2 text-text-primary whitespace-nowrap" style={`left:${BAR * 100}%`}>0.60 bar</span>
      <span class="float-right">1.0</span>
    </div>
    <p class="m-0 mt-2 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      The bar is <code>judge.calibration.AUTOMATION_BAR</code>, 0.60, the floor of Landis and Koch's
      "substantial". Nothing stands against it. A <code>JudgeContract</code> carrying no
      <code>CalibrationRecord</code> is unlicensed by construction and <code>require_licensed()</code>
      refuses, so the code cannot quietly treat a chosen judge as a calibrated one.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-4" role="group" aria-label="Choose the candidate family">
    <span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted mr-1" aria-hidden="true">Family:</span>
    <button type="button" class="jc-toggle on inline-flex items-center font-mono text-mono-xs px-3 min-h-11 border border-border-dark transition-colors" data-jc-arm="openai" aria-pressed="true">
      OpenAI
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="jc-toggle inline-flex items-center font-mono text-mono-xs px-3 min-h-11 border border-border-dark text-text-muted transition-colors" data-jc-arm="anthropic" aria-pressed="false">
      Anthropic
    </button>
  </div>

  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted">
    <span>candidate</span>
    <span class="w-32 text-right">selection set</span>
  </div>
  <ul class="grid gap-y-0 m-0 p-0 list-none" data-jc-rows>
    {
      arms.openai.rows.map((r) => (
        <li class="jc-row flex items-center justify-between gap-3 py-2 border-b border-border-dark/40">
          <span class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
            <span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-primary truncate" data-jc-model>{r.model}</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted truncate" data-jc-detail>{r.detail}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="w-32 text-right font-mono text-mono-xs shrink-0">
            <span class="jc-score" data-jc-score data-chosen={String(r.chosen)}>{r.score}/{arms.openai.trials}</span>
            <span class="block jc-verdict-tag" data-jc-tag>{r.chosen ? 'chosen' : 'rejected'}</span>
          </span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <p class="m-0 mt-3 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted" aria-hidden="true">
    ground truth by construction, never a human label · 10 PASS / 10 FAIL, so an always PASS judge scores 50%
  </p>

  <figcaption class="m-0 mt-4 font-mono text-mono-xs text-text-muted leading-relaxed" data-jc-caption aria-live="polite">
    OpenAI arm: every case under both prompt conditions, so 40 verdicts per candidate. gpt-5.6-luna took
    40 of 40 and was the cheapest of the four that tied at the top; gpt-5.4-mini took 36 of 40 and came
    last of the nine candidates run. Across all 360 calls in the sweep, 11 verdicts were wrong and
    <span class="text-error">10 of those 11 were a false FAIL on a PASS case</span>. The judges err in one
    direction, and both rejected candidates missed the same case, a correct claim carrying a wrong
    citation, so the over harshness is shared across families rather than being one vendor's quirk.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style is:global>
  /* selection state is neutral ink, never the green accent; green is reserved for the good/passing
     data state so the accent means one thing in this figure. */
  [data-jc] .jc-toggle.on {
    border-color: var(--color-text-primary);
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-text-primary) 6%, transparent);
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-licence {
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-error) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-error) 4%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-licence code { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  [data-jc] .jc-track {
    background: var(--color-surface-container-high);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-dark);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-bar {
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-score[data-chosen='true'] {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-score[data-chosen='false'] {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-verdict-tag {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  [data-jc] .jc-row.changed {
    animation: jc-pulse 0.9s var(--ease-out-quint);
  }
  @keyframes jc-pulse {
    from { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 14%, transparent); }
    to { background: transparent; }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    [data-jc] .jc-row.changed { animation: none; }
  }
</style>
